(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA) '
(MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS & MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT) '
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: PRADHAN MANTRI AWAS YOJANA [PMAY] - HOUSING FOR ALL) '
T*
(1. SCHEME OVERVIEW AND OBJECTIVE) '
(The Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana [PMAY] was launched in June 2015 with the overarching ) '
(objective of providing 'Housing for All' across urban and rural India. The scheme ) '
(aims to construct 2.95 crore pucca houses equipped with basic amenities including ) '
(water supply, electricity connection, sanitation facility [toilet], and clean cooking ) '
(fuel connections [LPG under PM Ujjwala Yojana] by the target year 2025.) '
T*
(2. SCHEME COMPONENTS AND COVERAGE) '
(The mission covers two broad verticals:) '
(a] Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - Urban [PMAY-U]: Implemented across all 4,372 ) '
(statutory towns in India, addressing the affordable housing shortage among the urban ) '
(poor including Economically Weaker Sections [EWS], Low Income Groups [LIG], and ) '
(Middle Income Groups [MIG].) '
(b] Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - Gramin [PMAY-G]: Implemented across all rural ) '
(districts in India to provide financial assistance to rural households living in ) '
(kutcha, dilapidated, or roofless houses identified via the Socio-Economic and Caste ) '
(Census [SECC 2011].) '
T*
(3. FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE AND SUBSIDY STRUCTURE) '
(- Rural Assistance [PMAY-G]: Direct benefit transfer [DBT] of ?1.20 Lakh per unit in ) '
(plain areas and ?1.30 Lakh per unit in hilly, North-Eastern, and difficult Himalayan ) '
(terrain areas. Additionally, beneficiaries receive 90/95 days of unskilled labor wage ) '
(support under MGNREGS [approx ?25,000] and ?12,000 for toilet construction under ) '
(Swachh Bharat Mission [SBM-G].) '
(- Urban Assistance [PMAY-U]: Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme [CLSS] provides upfront ) '
(interest subsidy of up to 6.5% for loans up to ?6.00 Lakh for EWS/LIG categories, ) '
(delivering interest relief of up to ?2.67 Lakh over a loan tenure of up to 20 years.) '
T*
(4. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA) '
(- The beneficiary family must not own a pucca house [all-weather dwelling unit] ) '
(either in their name or in the name of any member of their family in any part of ) '
(India.) '
(- EWS households with annual household income up to ?3.00 Lakh.) '
(- LIG households with annual household income between ?3.00 Lakh and ?6.00 Lakh.) '
(- MIG-I households with annual household income between ?6.00 Lakh and ?12.00 Lakh.) '
(- Mandatory ownership or co-ownership by female head of the family in urban ) '
(allotments to promote women empowerment.) '
T*
(5. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS FOR APPLICATION) '
(- Aadhaar Card of all family members.) '
(- Valid Income Certificate / BPL Ration Card / Salary Slip.) '
(- Bank Account Details [Account Number, IFSC code, linked with Aadhaar for DBT].) '
(- Proof of Address [Voter ID, Electricity bill, Water bill].) '
(- Affidavit declaring non-ownership of any pucca house in India.) '
(- Land title deed or allotment letter [for beneficiary-led individual construction].) '
T*
(6. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND NODAL AGENCY) '
(Citizens can apply online via the official national portal at https://pmaymis.gov.in ) '
([for Urban] or https://pmayg.nic.in [for Rural] or offline through Common Service ) '
(Centres [CSCs] and local Municipal Corporation / Gram Panchayat offices.) '
(- Nodal Agencies: Housing and Urban Development Corporation [HUDCO], National Housing ) '
(Bank [NHB], and State Level Nodal Agencies [SLNA].) '
(- National Toll-Free Helpline: 1800-11-6163 / 1800-11-3377.) '
ET
